messages:
devin: Heads-up — I'm about to land a Terraform refactor that hoists provider blocks into the root module and centralizes required_providers. Goal is to remove duplicated provider pins across modules and have one canonical .terraform.lock.hcl. Plan: add root `required_providers` and *not* run `-upgrade` in my first PR. If that looks good I'll regenerate the lockfile in CI with the vetted terraform image. Any objections?

sara: Quick Q — if we don't run `-upgrade` can we still accidentally pull different provider versions from CI runners? want a clear rollback path.

devin: Good call. I plan to add explicit version ranges in the root `required_providers` (so CI deterministic), and then regenerate the lockfile using the same terraform binary we use in CI. Rollback = revert the hoist PR; modules still have their provider references but root will be removed.

arik: Can you paste the exact `required_providers` block you're adding? makes review easier.

devin: Sure — here's the block I'll add to root `versions.tf`:

```
terraform {
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = ">= 4.50, < 5.0"
    }
    kubernetes = {
      source  = "hashicorp/kubernetes"
      version = ">= 2.9, < 3.0"
    }
  }
}
```

olivia: FYI CI on my branch failed earlier with: `Error: provider registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/kubernetes v2.6.1: checksum mismatch` — I suspect a lockfile/platform mismatch. We should generate the lockfile via the same CI image and add `-platform=linux_amd64` if needed.

mike: Also +1 for adding a smoke job. Suggest infra-ci matrix: run `terraform init && terraform plan` against staging for the infra root and one critical module after the lockfile regen. I can add that.

devin: Sounds good. To minimize blast radius I'll: 1) open PR that only hoists the blocks (no `-upgrade`), 2) add the explicit ranges above, 3) update CI to regenerate the lockfile with the official TF image and platform flag, 4) coordinate smoke job from mike. Olivia can re-run her branch after that.

sara: ping me on the PR for a quick review. also add a note in the PR description about the rollback steps.

devin: will do. tagging @arik @olivia @mike for visibility. :thumbsup:

ci-bot: terraform/plan — success — no changes detected (run by dev-ci, image: hashicorp/terraform:1.5.7)

arik: thanks — that plan output looks clean. I'll watch the PR for the provider block diff and the lockfile commit. :eyes:
